      "body": "\n\n## Overview\n\nKimi-Linear fails at startup with `--mamba-ssm-cache-dtype bfloat16`. Same bug as #59147 (GLM-5.3-Flash), in the KDA layer Kimi-Linear uses (`KimiGatedDeltaNetAttention`).\n\n## Claims\n\n- Kimi-Linear starts and serves with `--mamba-ssm-cache-dtype bfloat16`. On main it hits `assert self.page_size_padded >= page_size` during engine init.\n- Default (`auto`, float32 state) is unchanged.\n- With the bf16 state, GSM8K is within 2 questions of the float32 state, and the KV cache holds 47% more tokens on 1xH200.\n\n## Validation\n\nUnit test, red/green (L40S):\n\n```bash\npytest tests/models/kimi_k3/test_kda.py -k \"kimi_linear_kda_state_dtype or recoverssm_config or warmup_skips\"\n```\n\nmain: `1 failed, 4 passed` (the bf16 case gets a float32 layer state). This PR: `5 passed`.\n\nE2E with dummy weights (1xL40S): `moonshotai/Kimi-Linear-48B-A3B-Instruct --load-format dummy`, 4 layers (3 KDA + 1 MLA) via `hf_overrides`, a 3000-token prompt with `max_num_batched_tokens=1024` so prefill is chunked and reads the cached state.\n\n| `--mamba-ssm-cache-dtype` | mode | main | this PR |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| auto | eager | generates | generates |\n| bfloat16 | eager | `AssertionError` in `MambaSpec.page_size_bytes` | generates |\n| bfloat16 | CUDA graphs | - | generates |\n\nThe unit test and the \"this PR\" column were rerun after rebasing onto current main, with the same results.\n\nReal weights, 1xH200, `LLM(..., max_model_len=8192, gpu_memory_utilization=0.9)`, GSM8K 5-shot, 1319 questions, via `tests/evals/gsm8k/gsm8k_eval.py::evaluate_gsm8k_offline`:\n\n| `--mamba-ssm-cache-dtype` | this PR on current main | before rebasing onto #60502 (2 runs) | attn block size | KV cache tokens |\n|---|---|---|---|---|\n| auto (fp32 state) | 0.8961 | 0.8961, 0.8961 | 1920 | 1,428,386 |\n| bfloat16 | 0.8976 | 0.8999, 0.8999 | 1024 | 2,104,173 |\n\n#60502 landed while I was testing and rewrote the KDA chunk kernels, so I reran after rebasing. Main can't run bfloat16 at all, so there is no main column.\n\n`pre-commit` passes.\n\n## Details\n\n`KimiLinearForCausalLM.get_mamba_state_dtype_from_config` passes `mamba_ssm_cache_dtype`, but `KimiGatedDeltaNetAttention.get_state_dtype` did not. The hybrid block-size alignment uses the model-level dtype (bf16), so `mamba_page_size_padded` is sized for a bf16 state, while the layer's `MambaSpec` is built with a float32 state that is about twice as large.\n\nPassing the dtype exposed a second issue: `chunk_kda_with_fused_gate` returns a float32 final state, and the prefill write-back `recurrent_state[idx] = last_recurrent_state` fails with `Index put requires the source and destination dtypes match`. This PR casts it to the cache dtype, the same as the Kimi-K3 KDA layer does after the same kernel. The decode kernels already cast on store.\n\nKimi-K3 is not affected: its KDA layer (`KimiK3DeltaAttention`) already passes the dtype.\n\nROCm: this layer is shared, but `amd/linear.py` still drops the flag at the model level. #58743 changes that line, so this PR leaves it alone. Until then, on ROCm with this flag the layer uses a bf16 state padded to the float32 page size, so it does not hit the assert. Not tested on ROCm.\n\nNot a duplicate: searched open and closed PRs and issues for Kimi-Linear / `mamba_ssm_cache_dtype` / KDA state dtype. #59147 fixed only GLM-5.3-Flash, and #58743 covers only the ROCm Kimi-K3 path.\n\nAI assistance (Claude Code) was used to find the bug, write the change and run the validation above.\n\n---\n\n<details>\n<summary> Pull Request Checklist </summary>\n\n- [x] I used vLLM's `/pr-checklist` skill. (Mandatory for agents, optional for humans).\n- [x] AI assistance was used during the creation of this PR.\n\n- [x] **Design Fit:** Minimizes impact on core components, reuses existing functionality, and justifies added complexity.\n- [x] **Testing and Validation:** Validates the change and ensures any added tests are meaningful and reliable, with CI coverage or documented CI resource constraints and validation performed outside CI.\n- [x] **Code Quality and Style:** Keeps code and comments clear and concise, and updates relevant documentation and examples.\n- [x] **Pull Request Contents:** Includes a brief summary and relevant links, supports claims with evidence, explains root causes and implementation trade-offs, and follows the contributing guide.\n</details>\n",
